Terrie Vasilopoulos is a collaborative biostatistician and an associate professor in the Departments of Anesthesiology and Orthopaedic Sur
gery & Sports Medicine at the University of Florida College of Medicine and serves as chief of the Department of Anesthesiology's Division
of Education Research and Scholarship. She holds a PhD in Biobehavioral Health from the Pennsylvania State University and Graduate Statis
tician Certification from the American Statistical Association.
Dmitry Tumin is an associate professor in Pediatrics at the Brody School of Medicine at East Carolina University and serves as the school's
Assistant Dean of Clinical and Educational Scholarship. He holds an MA and PhD in Sociology from the Ohio State University.
